{
  "source": "Prompts/critical-thinking-reroll-3.mp4",
  "duration": 194.6296875,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.48,
      "text": "Navigating information requires a two-part equation, combining your existing knowledge"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.48,
      "end": 7.76,
      "text": "with an active way of processing it."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.34,
      "end": 10.24,
      "text": "On the left, we have your baseline knowledge."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.86,
      "end": 15.6,
      "text": "This background context helps you understand a subject and provides the perspective necessary"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.6,
      "end": 18.26,
      "text": "to recognize when something doesn't add up."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.84,
      "end": 20.12,
      "text": "You then add critical thinking."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.88,
      "end": 26.04,
      "text": "This is the process where you question a claim, examine the evidence, and consider other explanations"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.4,
      "end": 28.48,
      "text": "before deciding what to believe or do."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.48,
      "end": 32.24,
      "text": "This combination leads to better questions and better decisions."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.98,
      "end": 35.46,
      "text": "Your goal is to be smarter than the tool."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.24,
      "end": 37.9,
      "text": "This approach avoids blind distrust."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.58,
      "end": 43.02,
      "text": "Instead, it relies on the habit of asking exactly what conditions would have to be met"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.02,
      "end": 44.98,
      "text": "for a specific claim to hold up."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.66,
      "end": 49.56,
      "text": "In 2015, headlines around the world announced a delicious discovery."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.4,
      "end": 53.04,
      "text": "A new study showed that eating chocolate helps you lose weight."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.78,
      "end": 55.64,
      "text": "Slim by chocolate ran one front page."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.64,
      "end": 57.74,
      "text": "That headline should make you pause."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.38,
      "end": 63.24,
      "text": "That hesitation is the start of critical thinking, which leads you to ask whether the evidence"
    },
    {
      "start": 63.24,
      "end": 64.76,
      "text": "actually supports the claim."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.5,
      "end": 68.44,
      "text": "When this news broke, reactions went in two different directions."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.2,
      "end": 70.5,
      "text": "There's the face-value reaction."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.28,
      "end": 71.66,
      "text": "Sounds great."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.02,
      "end": 72.48,
      "text": "I believe it."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.24,
      "end": 74.86,
      "text": "Then there's the critical thinking reaction."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.64,
      "end": 77.16,
      "text": "Wait, what's behind the claim?"
    },
    {
      "start": 77.86,
      "end": 82.6,
      "text": "You must actively pause and evaluate whenever a claim sounds exactly like what you want"
    },
    {
      "start": 82.6,
      "end": 82.98,
      "text": "to believe."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.98,
      "end": 86.86,
      "text": "The chocolate study was real, but it was deliberately flimsy."
    },
    {
      "start": 87.38,
      "end": 90.06,
      "text": "The entire group consisted of only 15 participants."
    },
    {
      "start": 90.86,
      "end": 95.66,
      "text": "To create the desired result, they measured 18 different things about those 15 people."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.22,
      "end": 100.46,
      "text": "With that many measurements in such a small group, a chance result could look like an important"
    },
    {
      "start": 100.46,
      "end": 100.94,
      "text": "discovery."
    },
    {
      "start": 101.82,
      "end": 102.84,
      "text": "The deception went deeper."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.48,
      "end": 107.88,
      "text": "The Research Institute was a website created for the project, and the author was a journalist"
    },
    {
      "start": 107.88,
      "end": 111.96,
      "text": "testing if a bad study with a great headline would go viral unchecked."
    },
    {
      "start": 111.96,
      "end": 117.48,
      "text": "The study flew around the world because no one checked the underlying data, confirming"
    },
    {
      "start": 117.48,
      "end": 118.64,
      "text": "the journalist's point."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.36,
      "end": 124.3,
      "text": "True critical thinking requires the ability to read between the lines and inspect the source,"
    },
    {
      "start": 124.9,
      "end": 127.08,
      "text": "especially when the claim is incredibly appealing."
    },
    {
      "start": 128.0,
      "end": 131.44,
      "text": "You can sharpen your critical thinking by building five specific habits."
    },
    {
      "start": 132.26,
      "end": 133.76,
      "text": "Each one is a question you ask."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.68,
      "end": 134.98,
      "text": "Habit one."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.64,
      "end": 136.48,
      "text": "Is it actually right?"
    },
    {
      "start": 137.16,
      "end": 140.76,
      "text": "Ask what evidence supports the claim, and if it truly supports the conclusion."
    },
    {
      "start": 141.42,
      "end": 142.16,
      "text": "Habit two."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.66,
      "end": 143.86,
      "text": "Do I know enough to judge?"
    },
    {
      "start": 144.8,
      "end": 148.22,
      "text": "Recognize where your knowledge ends and find out what you need to understand."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.08,
      "end": 149.58,
      "text": "Habit three."
    },
    {
      "start": 150.12,
      "end": 150.54,
      "text": "What's missing?"
    },
    {
      "start": 151.22,
      "end": 153.48,
      "text": "Look for missing information and other explanations."
    },
    {
      "start": 154.5,
      "end": 155.12,
      "text": "Habit four."
    },
    {
      "start": 155.68,
      "end": 156.44,
      "text": "Why am I convinced?"
    },
    {
      "start": 157.22,
      "end": 161.96,
      "text": "Determine if your belief is based on the evidence, the confident wording, or simply what you"
    },
    {
      "start": 161.96,
      "end": 162.48,
      "text": "want to believe."
    },
    {
      "start": 163.12,
      "end": 163.8,
      "text": "Habit five."
    },
    {
      "start": 164.34,
      "end": 164.92,
      "text": "What's my call?"
    },
    {
      "start": 165.64,
      "end": 169.64,
      "text": "Decide what to believe or do, and remember that you can change your mind when you learn"
    },
    {
      "start": 169.64,
      "end": 169.86,
      "text": "more."
    },
    {
      "start": 170.56,
      "end": 173.36,
      "text": "These five questions work on anything you read or hear."
    },
    {
      "start": 174.14,
      "end": 176.08,
      "text": "You should use these same questions with AI."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.2,
      "end": 180.96,
      "text": "AI can help you find a flaw in your thinking, or confidently repeat it."
    },
    {
      "start": 181.44,
      "end": 182.92,
      "text": "You need to judge which is happening."
    },
    {
      "start": 183.8,
      "end": 185.76,
      "text": "These banners summarize the core relationship."
    },
    {
      "start": 186.7,
      "end": 188.78,
      "text": "AI amplifies whatever you bring to it."
    },
    {
      "start": 188.78,
      "end": 191.0,
      "text": "Good thinking in, sharper output."
    }
  ],
